<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cayster River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Küçük Menderes, Kaystros, Cayster</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cayster, now the Küçük Menderes, is a river in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> that flows into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aegean">Aegean</a> near the ruins of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephesus">Ephesus</a>. The ancient city was founded near its mouth, but the silt the river carried steadily filled the harbour and pushed the coastline westwards, so that Ephesus was eventually left several kilometres inland and lost its role as a port.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cayster-river.jpg" alt="Cayster River" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: dsdwn · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:K%C3%BC%C3%A7%C3%BCk_Menderes_1.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
